# ── Supabase ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create a project at https://supabase.com, then copy these from
# Project Settings → API. Public (browser-safe) keys are prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-anon-public-key"

# Server-only. NEVER expose to the browser — do not prefix it NEXT_PUBLIC_, or
# Next.js inlines it into the JavaScript bundle every visitor downloads.
#
# This key skips every RLS policy, so it is only used where RLS cannot reach:
# `auth.users`, via lib/supabase/admin.ts. That powers the members directory's
# "Never signed in" column and its two repairs — confirm a member's address, or
# correct one that was mistyped. Everything else uses the anon key plus RLS.
#
# Optional. Without it the directory still lists members and verification still
# works; only the login-state column and those two repairs switch off.
# Copy from Project Settings → API → service_role (Reveal).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="your-service-role-key"

# ── App ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The site's own origin, and the single thing a domain move changes. Read through
# lib/site.ts, which every metadata tag, canonical URL, sitemap entry, robots
# directive and auth email link derives from.
#
# Production: https://bekwaiyouthmovement.org
# Local dev:  http://localhost:3000
# Previews:   leave unset — lib/site.ts falls back to VERCEL_URL, so a preview
#             deployment generates links to itself rather than to production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Supabase Send Email Hook ──────────────────────────────
# Lets our backend send Supabase's auth email (confirm signup, password reset,
# magic link, invite, email change) instead of Supabase sending it — see
# app/api/auth/send-email/route.ts and supabase/README.md §4a.
#
# Generate it at Authentication → Hooks → Send Email Hook, and paste the WHOLE
# value including the "v1,whsec_" prefix; lib/webhook-signature.ts strips it.
#
# This must be set in Vercel, not only here: the hook posts to the deployed site.
# Without it every hook request is rejected with 401 and no auth email is sent —
# which, with "Confirm email" on, means nobody can register.
SEND_EMAIL_HOOK_SECRET="v1,whsec_your_secret_here"

# ── Email — BYM's own mail server (preferred) ─────────────
# lib/email.ts uses SMTP when these are set, and falls back to Resend only if
# they are not. Preferred because mail leaves an address the movement controls,
# there is no third-party quota to exhaust mid-drive, and no external account
# that can be suspended and take registration with it.
#
# Credentials are the cPanel mailbox's own — cPanel → Email Accounts →
# Connect Devices shows them. The mailbox must exist before this works.
#
# SMTP_HOST: use the server hostname, NOT mail.bekwaiyouthmovement.org, until the
# MX/A fix in DOMAIN.md §2 is done — that name still resolves to Vercel, which
# runs no mail server, so it would time out.
SMTP_HOST="s44.srvx.ws"
SMTP_PORT="465"                 # 465 = implicit TLS. 587 = STARTTLS.
SMTP_USER="info@bekwaiyouthmovement.org"
SMTP_PASS="the mailbox password"
# SMTP_SECURE is inferred from the port (465 -> true). Only set it to override.
# SMTP_SECURE="true"

# ── Email (Resend) — fallback ─────────────────────────────
# Optional, and only for the app's OWN notifications (contact alerts, newsletter
# broadcasts, application updates). When unset the app still works — messages
# save to the Inbox, broadcasts save as drafts.
#
# This is NOT how members get their confirm-your-email and reset-password mail.
# That is Supabase Auth over the SMTP provider set in the dashboard (Brevo) —
# see supabase/README.md §4a. Leaving this unset does not affect sign-up.
#
# Resend requires a DNS-verified sending domain. BYM now has one, so this is
# finally switchable on:
#   1. https://resend.com → Domains → add bekwaiyouthmovement.org
#   2. Add the SPF/DKIM records it shows you to the domain's DNS
#   3. Wait for "Verified", then create an API key → RESEND_API_KEY
#   4. Set EMAIL_FROM to an address AT that domain (below)
#
# Until RESEND_API_KEY is set, emailEnabled() is false and every caller degrades
# quietly: registration still works, the welcome email is skipped, applications
# still submit, broadcasts save as drafts. Nothing breaks — it is just silent.
RESEND_API_KEY="re_your_key_here"

# A *sender*, and it must be at the DNS-verified domain. A gmail.com address here
# is rejected outright, whoever owns it.
EMAIL_FROM="Bekwai Youth Movement <info@bekwaiyouthmovement.org>"

# Where the Secretariat is notified, and the Reply-To on member mail.
#
# OPTIONAL, and set deliberately. Leave it unset and mail goes to the role
# mailbox (info@bekwaiyouthmovement.org) — the right answer for the Movement.
# Set it to a person's address to route notifications to whoever is actually
# running the system day to day.
#
# Live until December 2026: set in Vercel to the founder's personal address,
# because during the build-out notifications need to reach someone who reads
# them hourly. Handover is deleting this variable — see supabase/README.md §4c-i.
EMAIL_ADMIN="rmensahuk@gmail.com"
